WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.960
Hey I'm Kennedy for Reason TV,

00:00:01.960 --> 00:00:03.100
I got kids,

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:05.480
during the holidays I like to sit down with
my girls

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:08.340
and watch some family friendly freedom focused
films

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:09.800
about Christmas cheer.

00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:13.500
And when I'm chuggin' my 100 proof gluten-free
eggnog

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:16.680
I want to make sure my girls are mainlining
liberty.

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:20.260
So, with the help of Reason film critic and
my good friend Kurt Loder,

00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:24.560
we put together a list of classic holiday
movies to avoid and to imbibe

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:28.420
all to help you enjoy a responsible Libertarian
Christmas.

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:31.220
First up, the cinematic lumps of coal.

00:00:31.220 --> 00:00:33.100
A Charlie Brown Christmas,

00:00:33.110 --> 00:00:36.629
the titular blockhead is offended by the commercialization of Christmas

00:00:36.629 --> 00:00:39.329
which is a neat trick to pull off during a
Christmas special

00:00:39.329 --> 00:00:41.880
sponsored by Dolly Madison snack cakes.

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:43.010
'I don't care.'

00:00:43.010 --> 00:00:46.239
Poor little Charlie Brown is clearly an enemy
of capitalism,

00:00:46.239 --> 00:00:49.120
who probably grows up to join occupy hell.

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:50.760
'Everything I touch gets ruined.'

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:54.049
A Christmas Memory propagates the un-Libertarian
idea

00:00:54.049 --> 00:00:56.960
that getting blind drunk during the holidays
is somehow wrong.

00:00:56.960 --> 00:00:58.980
'Are you out of your mind?'

00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:02.660
Love Actually propagates the un-Libertarian
idea that getting blind drunk

00:01:02.660 --> 00:01:05.560
and watching porn during the holidays is somehow
wrong-

00:01:05.560 --> 00:01:06.260
'Rubbish'

00:01:06.260 --> 00:01:09.320
White Christmas, two showbiz sisters, played
by Vera-Ellen

00:01:09.320 --> 00:01:11.280
and George Clooney's aunt Rosemary,

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:15.620
destroy an expensive rug that is the private
property of their landlord.

00:01:15.620 --> 00:01:20.320
Instead of making the ethically necessary
restitution, they run out on this obligation.

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:22.740
This is offensive, and not just for Libertarians.

00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:28.300
Miracle on 34th Street, actor Kris Kringle
is dispatched to the nervous hospital

00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:30.700
for insisting that he's really Santa Claus,

00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:33.360
the post office saves the day, 'nuff said.

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:35.240
'You're making a mistake.'

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:37.040
FedEx woulda sprung him overnight.

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:40.480
Now to be fair there was some debate about
this movie in the Reason office,

00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:42.400
with Mike Riggs quick to point out

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:45.560
it's one of his favorite pro-Libertarian Christmas movies

00:01:45.560 --> 00:01:47.460
because it exposes government corruption

00:01:47.469 --> 00:01:51.720
and showcases the horrors of involuntary commitment.

00:01:51.720 --> 00:01:55.900
Now here are the good Libertarian Christmas
movies, we need this, right?

00:01:55.900 --> 00:01:58.220
My favorite is Rudolph the Red-Nosed Reindeer.

00:01:58.220 --> 00:01:59.560
Oh Rudolph!

00:01:59.560 --> 00:02:03.899
Rudolph's distinguishing characteristic is
universally seen as a deformity

00:02:03.899 --> 00:02:07.369
and he's outcast from the reindeer games and
the herd.

00:02:07.369 --> 00:02:13.220
Yet, through self examination and reinvention,
he turns his perceived impairment into an asset

00:02:13.220 --> 00:02:15.700
and becomes the most popular reindeer of all
time.

00:02:15.710 --> 00:02:18.030
In the process he saves his gal and his parents

00:02:18.030 --> 00:02:21.680
and befriends precious metal loving prospector
Yukon Cornelius.

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:24.080
'I'm off to get my life sustaining supplies,

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:27.100
cornmeal and gunpowder and ham hocks and guitar
strings.'

00:02:27.100 --> 00:02:31.960
Then there's the brief moment in the sentimental
holiday standard It's A Wonderful Life,

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:34.690
when bankster George Bailey travels to Pottersville,

00:02:34.690 --> 00:02:39.210
the place his home town of Bedford Falls would
have become if he'd never been born.

00:02:39.210 --> 00:02:41.300
Now we only see Pottersville for a few moments,

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:45.160
but it looks to be a city comprised solely
of whore houses and gin mills,

00:02:45.160 --> 00:02:46.320
which is pretty awesome.

00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:47.980
'Hee-haw and merry Christmas.'

00:02:47.980 --> 00:02:51.240
My other holiday favorite, which is not itself
a Christmas movie

00:02:51.240 --> 00:02:53.600
but has become one over the years by default,

00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:56.960
is The Sound of Music which is endlessly lovable.

00:02:56.960 --> 00:03:00.620
How could you not adore a plucky, anti-authoritarian
nun,

00:03:00.630 --> 00:03:05.450
who's a thorn in the side of the church and
the loins of the tyrannical naval captain

00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:08.600
whom she wins over despite making lederhosen
out of green drapes.

00:03:09.910 --> 00:03:14.200
That she also takes down the entire Nazi regime,
yeah just gravy really.

00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:16.680
Now which other movies deserve to make it
on our list?

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:21.120
Anti-Libertarian holiday movies have no place in a
freedom friendly family room,

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:22.612
always looking out for you.

00:03:22.620 --> 00:03:24.540
For Reason TV, I'm Kennedy.

